WEBVTT

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.980
That's right. He's my older brother.

00:00:07.650 --> 00:00:08.980
<b>Monkfish Baths</b>

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:12.620
I knew it. I thought you looked like him.

00:00:12.620 --> 00:00:13.990
Your last names are different, though.

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:16.740
A lot of things have happened.

00:00:16.740 --> 00:00:20.640
Though I may dive into 
the water, I will not pry...

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.100
Lots can happen in life...

00:00:24.030 --> 00:00:27.180
Lots of different kinds of waves, too...

00:00:41.350 --> 00:00:42.640
I...

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:43.850
I'm flying!

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:49.180
<i>It felt amazing!</i>

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.980
<i>I'll never get enough!</i>

00:00:52.490 --> 00:00:54.440
Hey, Corgi?

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:58.130
Corgi!

00:00:58.130 --> 00:00:58.930
Huh?

00:01:00.170 --> 00:01:01.200
What are you doing?

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.450
It's 'cuz you were spacing out.

00:01:03.450 --> 00:01:04.650
Are you tired?

00:01:04.650 --> 00:01:06.360
Not at all! I'm fine!

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.680
Tomorrow morning, let's go surfing again!

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.400
Oh, looks like you're raring to go.

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:14.510
Which is a huge difference 
from how you've been up to now.

00:01:14.510 --> 00:01:15.970
My older brother...

00:01:16.590 --> 00:01:19.720
He said that surfing will change everything.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.910
It makes me happy that you've 
come to like surfing, Masaki.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:27.550
Yeah! I'm gonna practice more and more!

00:01:36.660 --> 00:01:37.990
<i>I didn't know...</i>

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:43.990
<i>To think that the ocean I saw every 
day might hold something so fun.</i>

00:01:44.630 --> 00:01:47.240
<i>Surfing will change everything.</i>

00:01:47.240 --> 00:01:48.350
<i>That's right.</i>

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.420
<i>Since the day I met Sho, 
the ocean that met my eyes</i>

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:55.630
<i>was completely different 
than it had been before.</i>

00:02:11.400 --> 00:02:15.900
Let's Go Surfing!!

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:34.810
2nd Wave The Ocean Will Tell You

00:03:38.120 --> 00:03:40.240
One, two, three!

00:03:49.510 --> 00:03:51.120
That's so weird.

00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:55.360
I did it so well yesterday.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.290
<i>The angle of your elbows when you paddle...</i>

00:04:01.290 --> 00:04:02.680
<i>Keep your chest up.</i>

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:05.450
<i>Reach as far out as you can 
to pull the water.</i>

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.890
This is good!

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.340
I want to feel...

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:17.150
<i>that feeling again!</i>

00:04:19.910 --> 00:04:21.190
<i>Watch the timing...</i>

00:04:21.550 --> 00:04:23.940
<i>One, two, three!</i>

00:04:37.740 --> 00:04:39.100
Good morning, Masaki!

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:41.210
'Sup, Corgi.

00:04:41.210 --> 00:04:43.720
Sho! Tanaka! You're late!

00:04:44.550 --> 00:04:47.280
You're the one who's too early.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:52.470
It's good to go all out, 
but don't push yourself too hard, okay?

00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:54.300
I know.

00:04:55.080 --> 00:04:56.980
Come on, you two!

00:04:56.980 --> 00:04:58.050
Let's go!

00:05:05.280 --> 00:05:07.130
<i>The waves are nice today, too.</i>

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:38.520
Make sure you rinse it well, 
just like you're doing now.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:46.780
And don't use seawater. 
Use fresh water, okay?

00:05:47.370 --> 00:05:52.020
If you don't, the screws holding 
the fin in place will rust.

00:05:52.020 --> 00:05:53.290
Oh, I get it.

00:05:53.830 --> 00:05:55.990
Oh, Corgi.

00:05:55.990 --> 00:06:00.690
You also need to check to make sure 
your board hasn't been scratched.

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:06.190
The seawater can get in and 
cause cracks, you see.

00:06:06.190 --> 00:06:07.380
Oh!

00:06:07.800 --> 00:06:09.380
Say, Shoko.

00:06:09.380 --> 00:06:12.170
I'd like to buy this board and the wet suit.

00:06:12.170 --> 00:06:15.680
Those? You can try them out 
for longer if you want.

00:06:16.700 --> 00:06:17.920
These...

00:06:18.690 --> 00:06:20.690
These are the ones I like!

00:06:22.700 --> 00:06:24.430
Give him a break on the price.

00:06:24.430 --> 00:06:26.440
Thank you, sir!

00:06:29.130 --> 00:06:32.030
Looks like you've really 
fallen in love with surfing.

00:06:32.030 --> 00:06:33.200
I'm glad!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.200
Yeah!

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.560
I'm happy, too!

00:06:36.560 --> 00:06:37.620
No one asked you!

00:06:45.090 --> 00:06:48.720
<b>Examples of Bad Paddling</b>

00:06:51.470 --> 00:06:55.100
<b>Nothing is going to change
I Can't Quit</b>

00:06:56.040 --> 00:07:00.510
Make sure to... rotate from the shoulders...

00:07:07.230 --> 00:07:11.580
It really is... hard to... 
get my arms in this...

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:15.590
Got it.

00:07:19.990 --> 00:07:21.830
Okay! Let's go!

00:07:22.250 --> 00:07:24.820
Hey, wait! Corgi!

00:07:37.110 --> 00:07:40.110
Surfing isn't that easy!

00:07:40.110 --> 00:07:42.510
You have to practice over and over!

00:07:56.110 --> 00:07:57.630
I see.

00:07:57.630 --> 00:07:59.940
So that's how you do a duck dive.

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:09.340
The most important thing... is speed...

00:08:21.350 --> 00:08:23.470
Why did you come to my house?

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:24.730
What else were we supposed to do?

00:08:24.730 --> 00:08:27.860
Monkfish Baths is temporarily closed.

00:08:27.860 --> 00:08:30.740
If we went back home, 
we'd be late for school.

00:08:32.950 --> 00:08:33.740
Huh?

00:08:33.740 --> 00:08:36.540
Oh. Good morning, Sakura-chan.

00:08:38.220 --> 00:08:40.870
Sh-Sho-sama?

00:08:40.870 --> 00:08:42.790
Huh? Sakura?

00:08:43.460 --> 00:08:45.960
I don't have a piano.

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:48.160
"I don't have a piano."

00:08:48.540 --> 00:08:50.380
You don't speak English.

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.440
Hey, Sho, Masaki.

00:08:56.440 --> 00:08:57.370
Hello.

00:08:57.370 --> 00:08:58.510
Hello!

00:08:58.920 --> 00:09:03.520
Sho has really started 
to fit in here in Oarai.

00:09:03.520 --> 00:09:04.740
Me, too! Me, too!

00:09:04.740 --> 00:09:06.890
You still have a long way to go.

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:07.900
Why?

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:13.780
<b>Sho-sama
 Happy Birthday</b>

00:09:11.570 --> 00:09:18.220
Happy birthday to you! 
Happy birthday to you!

00:09:12.410 --> 00:09:13.780
Happy birthday, Sho!

00:09:14.880 --> 00:09:18.220
You made all of this for me, Sakura-chan?

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:21.540
M-Mom taught me.

00:09:18.220 --> 00:09:22.920
Happy birthday dear, Sho-sama!

00:09:21.540 --> 00:09:24.390
Mom is really good at cooking, so...

00:09:23.310 --> 00:09:29.030
Happy birthday to you!

00:09:24.390 --> 00:09:26.540
Sho, you must be pretty happy, huh?

00:09:27.030 --> 00:09:29.030
I really am.

00:09:29.030 --> 00:09:31.920
This is the first time anyone 
has celebrated with me like this.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:35.300
The first time? It's always 
like this in our family.

00:09:35.300 --> 00:09:38.150
That's really a wonderful thing.

00:09:39.290 --> 00:09:40.540
Thank you.

00:09:43.560 --> 00:09:45.560
<b>Sho-sama
 Happy Birthday</b>

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.110
Happy birthday, Sho!

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:50.180
Happy birthday, Sho, happy birthday...

00:09:52.820 --> 00:09:54.070
Okay!

00:09:58.110 --> 00:09:59.820
Take off!

00:10:00.580 --> 00:10:02.450
Yahoo!

00:10:03.200 --> 00:10:05.130
He improves quickly.

00:10:05.130 --> 00:10:07.920
His sense of balance is incredible.

00:10:07.920 --> 00:10:09.730
It's the waves that are good.

00:10:11.080 --> 00:10:17.220
I never imagined that Corgi 
would work this hard at surfing.

00:10:17.720 --> 00:10:21.800
Once you do it, you can't quit. 
That's just how surfing is.

00:10:21.800 --> 00:10:23.240
True.

00:10:24.730 --> 00:10:28.010
Masaki, now that he's got the bottom turn,

00:10:28.010 --> 00:10:30.480
we should have him start 
practicing off the lip.

00:10:31.430 --> 00:10:32.230
What?

00:10:35.900 --> 00:10:37.070
A floater?

00:10:37.070 --> 00:10:39.910
Sho! Tanaka! Did you see that just now?

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:48.170
So, it's called a floater?

00:10:48.170 --> 00:10:49.900
It felt amazing!

00:10:50.630 --> 00:10:54.900
It was like... like I was one with the wave.

00:10:55.710 --> 00:10:59.720
The waves were good, 
but that was Joel Parkinson level!

00:10:59.720 --> 00:11:00.850
Right?

00:11:00.850 --> 00:11:02.900
It was just like Jojojo Pardinen, right?

00:11:02.900 --> 00:11:04.240
You have no idea, do you?

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:07.310
I'm gonna completely master it, 
like Pardinen, and...

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.890
Who is that supposed to be?

00:11:08.890 --> 00:11:13.480
That amazing feeling... 
I want to feel it again!

00:11:13.480 --> 00:11:16.020
I'm going to practice even harder!

00:11:17.090 --> 00:11:18.720
And one day...

00:11:20.230 --> 00:11:21.940
Just like Sho, I'll...

00:11:25.370 --> 00:11:26.370
Huh?

00:11:26.370 --> 00:11:28.550
N-Nothing.

00:11:28.550 --> 00:11:31.430
Masaki, it's good to be motivated,

00:11:31.430 --> 00:11:32.940
but you shouldn't push yourself too hard.

00:11:32.940 --> 00:11:35.440
Don't worry. I know.

00:11:35.440 --> 00:11:36.950
Do you really?

00:11:36.950 --> 00:11:38.380
Really, really.

00:11:39.110 --> 00:11:42.830
Masaki, you head for any wave that comes...

00:11:42.830 --> 00:11:45.510
But just going isn't enough.

00:11:45.510 --> 00:11:46.490
Huh?

00:11:47.040 --> 00:11:50.770
Waiting for a good wave. 
Picking the right wave and riding it.

00:11:51.360 --> 00:11:53.520
That's important, too.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:55.930
Really...

00:11:56.670 --> 00:12:00.560
I'll ride any wave that comes, though.

00:12:03.190 --> 00:12:06.960
<i>Day after day, I continued 
to practice my surfing.</i>

00:12:07.370 --> 00:12:10.690
<i>Even I could tell I was getting 
better, little by little,</i>

00:12:10.690 --> 00:12:13.770
<i>and every time I did, it was even more fun.</i>

00:12:14.120 --> 00:12:16.380
<i>Sho and Tanaka and me...</i>

00:12:16.380 --> 00:12:20.340
<i>I wanted those fun days to last forever.</i>

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:24.060
Excuse me.

00:12:22.990 --> 00:12:24.920
I see. So you've decided.

00:12:24.920 --> 00:12:26.540
Yes, Mr. Nogami.

00:12:26.540 --> 00:12:27.360
Murphy?

00:12:27.360 --> 00:12:30.540
I'll be taking an entrance exam 
for the Mid-Pacific Institute.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:33.140
That's the school in Hawaii 
you mentioned before, right?

00:12:34.900 --> 00:12:38.890
So you're planning to follow your father 
on the path to being a researcher?

00:12:38.890 --> 00:12:39.900
Yes.

00:12:40.310 --> 00:12:43.450
I'm thinking of specializing in geophysics.

00:12:43.450 --> 00:12:46.910
With your grades, 
I'm sure you'll be fine, but...

00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:50.450
You may want to try a little 
harder with your English.

00:12:50.450 --> 00:12:53.210
I'll try my best! I'll work hard.

00:12:53.210 --> 00:12:55.140
You've got some good waves waiting for you.

00:12:59.730 --> 00:13:01.100
Tanaka...

00:13:02.350 --> 00:13:05.990
When we graduate, he's going to Hawaii?

00:13:11.370 --> 00:13:14.980
<i>In his second year of middle school, 
he already knows where he's going next?</i>

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:18.190
<i>He's decided on his future.</i>

00:13:19.510 --> 00:13:22.820
<i>I wonder if the shape 
of the beach will change.</i>

00:13:24.600 --> 00:13:25.790
Sho!

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:27.320
Come on! Let's go!

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:30.920
According to the weather map, 
the offshore winds are strong!

00:13:31.450 --> 00:13:34.300
We're going to get some good offshore waves!

00:13:34.300 --> 00:13:36.480
It's the perfect weather for surfing!

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:41.950
Masaki, let's not go today.

00:13:44.220 --> 00:13:47.340
What are you talking about? 
Come on! Let's go!

00:13:47.340 --> 00:13:51.100
The show must go on! 
We have to keep surfing!

00:13:51.100 --> 00:13:52.350
No!

00:13:54.350 --> 00:13:57.380
What? You're no fun.

00:13:57.380 --> 00:14:00.060
Fine. I'll go by myself!

00:14:00.060 --> 00:14:00.980
Masaki!

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:02.980
Corgi?

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:20.110
<i>This looks impossible.</i>

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:22.500
<i>No.</i>

00:14:22.500 --> 00:14:23.630
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:14:39.390 --> 00:14:41.020
Okay! I can do this!

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:50.020
<i>This is bad!</i>

00:14:59.930 --> 00:15:01.200
<i>The shore...</i>

00:15:43.130 --> 00:15:44.400
Corgi...

00:15:54.790 --> 00:15:55.910
Corgi!

00:15:56.850 --> 00:15:58.940
I don't think he took in too much water.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:01.160
Really?

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:11.650
Masaki.

00:16:12.390 --> 00:16:13.510
Masaki?

00:16:20.870 --> 00:16:22.160
Sho.

00:16:36.480 --> 00:16:37.490
I—

00:16:38.350 --> 00:16:40.480
I told you not to push yourself too hard!

00:16:41.020 --> 00:16:42.980
Sh-Sho...

00:16:42.980 --> 00:16:45.080
There's nothing wrong with working hard!

00:16:45.080 --> 00:16:47.980
But working hard and 
recklessness are not the same!

00:16:47.980 --> 00:16:49.280
Do you understand?

00:16:53.140 --> 00:16:54.380
I'm sorry.

00:16:57.320 --> 00:17:00.120
<b>Monkfish Baths</b>

00:16:58.370 --> 00:17:00.140
About earlier...

00:17:00.740 --> 00:17:04.200
Thank you... for saving me...

00:17:04.620 --> 00:17:07.350
Don't worry about it. You just owe him one.

00:17:07.350 --> 00:17:09.470
Pay it back a hundredfold.

00:17:10.810 --> 00:17:11.940
Masaki.

00:17:13.150 --> 00:17:15.990
The reason I keep saying not to 
push yourself too hard...

00:17:15.990 --> 00:17:20.890
It's because they say that surfing 
is the sport closest to heaven.

00:17:21.750 --> 00:17:23.430
Heaven?

00:17:23.430 --> 00:17:24.510
That's why...

00:17:25.310 --> 00:17:30.520
Everyone practices hard and does all 
that training, so they don't die.

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:37.790
If anything happened to you, Masaki,

00:17:37.790 --> 00:17:40.210
a lot of people would be sad, right?

00:17:42.730 --> 00:17:44.540
I would be sad, too.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.160
Me, too. Me, too.

00:17:53.940 --> 00:17:56.800
Surfing is so much fun...

00:17:56.800 --> 00:17:57.750
Huh?

00:17:58.440 --> 00:18:00.050
I just...

00:18:00.880 --> 00:18:07.000
I just thought the three of us... 
would keep having fun like this.

00:18:07.740 --> 00:18:08.840
But...

00:18:09.810 --> 00:18:10.620
Huh?

00:18:10.620 --> 00:18:12.540
Tanaka, I think you're amazing.

00:18:12.540 --> 00:18:15.440
Wh-What's this all of a sudden? 
You're creeping me out.

00:18:15.800 --> 00:18:18.860
You're usually just a bum...

00:18:18.860 --> 00:18:21.830
But you've already decided on your career.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:27.190
Sorry. I overheard you talking 
to the teacher in the faculty office.

00:18:27.690 --> 00:18:32.070
Tanaka, you said you were going to 
a school in Hawaii after graduation.

00:18:33.270 --> 00:18:35.340
Wow. Hawaii?

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.360
I haven't decided anything yet.

00:18:39.070 --> 00:18:42.830
What I want to be... What I want to do...

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:45.790
I have no goals.

00:18:45.790 --> 00:18:49.950
I just that I wish I could keep 
surfing forever, that's all.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.510
I know it's in the future,

00:18:53.510 --> 00:18:58.020
but when I realized that after we
graduate we'll go our separate ways...

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:01.020
I just... I couldn't sit still.

00:19:02.110 --> 00:19:04.740
I wanted to surf together more.

00:19:05.490 --> 00:19:07.920
That's why today, I...

00:19:09.620 --> 00:19:11.260
Honestly.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:16.130
I'm sorry I didn't tell you.

00:19:16.700 --> 00:19:18.630
I was sort of embarrassed about it.

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:20.860
Tanaka...

00:19:21.480 --> 00:19:22.640
But!

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:28.270
Just because I go to Hawaii 
doesn't mean it's the end for us.

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:30.020
It's all one ocean.

00:19:30.020 --> 00:19:30.990
Huh?

00:19:30.990 --> 00:19:33.400
No matter where we go, 
we'll be in the same ocean.

00:19:34.200 --> 00:19:38.180
Even if we're apart, 
we'll be connected through surfing.

00:19:38.630 --> 00:19:40.570
Just like Sho says.

00:19:41.070 --> 00:19:44.110
Even if we can't see each other, 
the ocean will tell us...

00:19:44.910 --> 00:19:47.670
where the others are and what they're doing.

00:19:49.540 --> 00:19:52.250
So it isn't sad.

00:19:53.300 --> 00:19:54.940
Sho?

00:19:54.940 --> 00:19:59.170
Besides, Masaki, you have a 
perfectly good goal, don't you?

00:19:59.170 --> 00:19:59.920
Huh?

00:20:01.030 --> 00:20:04.800
Your goal is to become even 
better at surfing, right?

00:20:05.340 --> 00:20:07.640
My goal...

00:20:07.640 --> 00:20:10.330
We've still got a long time 
before we graduate.

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:18.820
We're going to be able to make lots 
and lots of good memories together.

00:20:19.360 --> 00:20:24.620
Just like the waves that break 
and keep coming one after another.

00:20:27.550 --> 00:20:29.100
Memories, huh?

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:32.790
That's it! Masaki! Tanaka.

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:34.580
How about we enter a competition together?

00:20:34.580 --> 00:20:36.060
A competition?

00:20:36.630 --> 00:20:40.320
Didn't you see the poster at Fantasy Island?

00:20:42.080 --> 00:20:45.830
Next summer, there's going to be 
a competition here in Oarai.

00:20:45.830 --> 00:20:47.470
Let's enter it!

00:20:47.470 --> 00:20:49.120
A competition...

00:20:49.640 --> 00:20:51.000
A competition?

00:20:52.490 --> 00:20:56.730
The timing works out so it'll be one year 
since you started surfing, Masaki.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:20:58.730
Let's do that competition!

00:20:58.730 --> 00:20:59.650
Okay!

00:20:59.650 --> 00:21:01.060
Right, Tanaka?

00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:03.270
A competition, huh?

00:21:03.270 --> 00:21:05.490
You'll be in it, right, Murphy?

00:21:05.490 --> 00:21:09.140
I'm not really a competitor... 
I'm more free—

00:21:12.430 --> 00:21:14.320
The summer of our third 
